### Introduction to Exception Handle
Exception Handling:-
- Exception handling is a programming mechanism that lets you detect, manage, and respond to errors (exceptions) that occur during the execution of a program. 
- Instead of letting the program crash when something unexpected happens, you "catch" the error, handle it gracefully, and decide how to continue.
- Graceful termination of the program.
** Purpose of Exception Handling:-
   - Graceful termination of the program.
   try {
    // read data from file
    }
     catch(Exception e) {
     // use local file & continue to run rest of the program normally.

Exception:- 
- Is a runtime event or Condition such-as error or Unexpected situation- that occurs during the excution of a program and disrupts its normal flow of program.
** Purpose of Exception:-
- it is highly recommanded. if something get wrong we should in a position to handle the situation. highly recommanded the exception
### Program:- 
import java.util.Scanner;
public class Program1 {
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		try {
			Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
			System.out.println("Enter the value of a :");
			int a  = sc.nextInt();
			System.out.println("Enter the value of b :");
			int b = sc.nextInt();
			int c = a/b;
			System.out.println("Result is : " + c);
		} catch (Exception e) {
			System.out.println("Exception handled");
		}
	}
}
